tps://orcid.org/0009-0007-0586-7956",{"_":184,"when":185,"who":161},"Jonathan Prag revised on basis of preliminary autopsy","2026-09-25",[],[188,189],"Supplementum epigraphicum graecum, 1923-","Orsi, 1918, Gli scavi intorno a l'Athenaion di Siracusa negli anni 1912-1917",[191,192],"F2GG87EQ","6R3V46Z8",[194,195,196,21,27,31,197,198,199,200,198,201,202,124],"isic003012","i.sicily inscription 003012",{"_":5},"syracusae","siracusa","sicilia","sicily","museo archeologico regionale paolo orsi","ancient greek",{"title":204,"body":205,"divs":206,"editions":225,"images":235,"handnote":236,"deprecation":19},"ISic003012. I.Sicily inscription 003012","\u003Cdiv id=\"editions\">\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa, Jonathan Prag; edition source: autopsy Observed by Prag 2026-09-17, without full study\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"grc\">  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"divine\" data-text=\"Ἄρκος\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Ἄρκος\">\u003Cspan class=\"petraeligature\" title=\"Ligature: these characters are joined\">Ἄ͡ρ\u003C/span>κος\u003C/span>\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa, Jonathan Prag; edition source: autopsy Observed by Prag 2026-09-17, without full study\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"al1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"divine\" data-text=\"Ἄρκος\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Ἄρκος\">\u003Cspan class=\"petraeligature\" title=\"Ligature: these characters are joined\">Α͡Ρ\u003C/span>ΚΟΣ\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"facsimile-images\">\u003Ch2>Facsimile Images\u003C/h2>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"apparatus\">\u003Ch4>Apparatus criticus\u003C/h4>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan>  \u003Cspan>Text from autopsy\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"translation\">\u003Ch2>English translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">\u003Ca href=\"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3819-8537\">Jonathan Prag\u003C/a>\u003C/p>  \u003Cp>Arkos\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"commentary\">\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>Manganaro suggested that the text referred to Arkos, a personification of 'security' (the word also means 'bear', and occurs as a personal name). Orsi speculated on [Συ]ρακοσ[ιος] or [Ἱε]ρακος, but neither of these seems plausible, given that the ligature should render ΑΡ, not ΡΑ, and there would seem to be a vacat before the Α. The letter forms perhaps suggest a third century BCE date, given the combination of broken bar alpha and open sigma.\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"bibliography\">\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Orsi 1918 610-611 fig.205 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001700\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001700\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> Manganaro 1977 158-159 ph \u003C/li>\u003Cli> 1984 34.0982 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000796\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000796\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"handnote\">\u003Cp>Roughly carved, with broken bar alpha, seemingly in ligature with rho; kappa with moderately short arms; smaller omicron; somewhat open four bar sigma.\u003C/p> Line 1    Interlineation line 1 to 2    \u003C/div>\u003C