nathan Prag\u003C/a>\u003C/p>  \u003Cp>Arkos\u003C/p>  ",{"id":217,"html":218},"commentary","\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>Manganaro suggested that the text referred to Arkos, a personification of 'security' (the word also means 'bear', and occurs as a personal name). Orsi speculated on [Συ]ρακοσ[ιος] or [Ἱε]ρακος, but neither of these seems plausible, given that the ligature should render ΑΡ, not ΡΑ, and there would seem to be a vacat before the Α. The letter forms perhaps suggest a third century BCE date, given the combination of broken bar alpha and open sigma.\u003C/p>  ",{"id":220,"html":221},"bibliography","\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Orsi 1918 610-611 fig.205 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001700\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001700\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> Manganaro 1977 158-159 ph \u003C/li>\u003Cli> 1984 34.0982 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000796\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000796\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  ",{"id":223,"html":224},"license"," Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence.  ",[226,228,231,232],{"html":227},"Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa, Jonathan Prag; edition source: autopsy Observed by Prag 2026-09-17, without full study",{"id":229,"lang":124,"html":230},"edition-interpretive","\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"divine\" data-text=\"Ἄρκος\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Ἄρκος\">\u003Cspan class=\"petraeligature\" title=\"Ligature: these characters are joined\">Ἄ͡ρ\u003C/span>κος\u003C/span>\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>",{"html":227},{"id":233,"lang":124,"html":